---
const fanboys = [
  ["F", "for", "Gives a reason", "We stayed inside, for it was raining."],
  ["A", "and", "Adds information", "The sun was shining and the birds were singing."],
  ["N", "nor", "Adds another negative idea", "She didn’t smile, nor did she speak."],
  ["B", "but", "Shows contrast", "I wanted to go outside, but it was raining."],
  ["O", "or", "Gives a choice", "Would you like tea or coffee?"],
  ["Y", "yet", "Shows contrast", "She was tired, yet she continued working."],
  ["S", "so", "Shows a result", "It was raining, so we stayed inside."]
];
---

<div class="topic-sheet">
  <h1>Conjunctions - Joining words and ideas</h1>
  <p>
    A <strong>conjunction</strong> connects words, phrases or clauses and shows how the ideas are related.
    “Tom <strong>and</strong> Sam went to the park.” “I wanted to go outside, <strong>but</strong> it was
    raining.” “We stayed inside <strong>because</strong> it was raining.”
  </p>
  <div class="summary-pair">
    <section class="summary-block summary-blue">
      <h2>Coordinating</h2>
      <p>Joins parts that are <strong>equal</strong>.</p>
      <p>The lights went out, <strong>but</strong> the torches still worked.</p>
      <p>Both ideas are main ideas. <em>But</em> shows the contrast.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="summary-block summary-mint">
      <h2>Subordinating</h2>
      <p>Introduces a <strong>subordinate</strong> idea.</p>
      <p>We used torches <strong>because</strong> it was dark.</p>
      <p><em>Because</em> marks the reason for the main idea.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
  <section class="summary-block summary-yellow">
    <h2>FANBOYS — the seven coordinating conjunctions</h2>
    <table class="punct-table summary-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="th-feature" scope="col">Letter</th>
          <th class="th-rule" scope="col">Word and job</th>
          <th class="th-example" scope="col">Example</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          fanboys.map(([letter, word, job, example]) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{letter}</th>
              <td>
                <strong>{word}</strong> — {job}
              </td>
              <td>{example}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
</div>
